Jules (Docs): opened a tiny PR to add short troubleshooting snippets for 429s + truncated streams. PR #8577.
Rex (Eng Docs): Keep examples micro: one header-retry snippet showing Retry-After then x-rw-retry, and one tiny streaming resume using resume_token + kv_cache_hint. No imports; add SDK version note.
Maya (SDK): Draft TS sample (TS SDK >=3.2):
```ts
// Retry-After preferred, fallback x-rw-retry
async function sendWithRetry(req){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const res = await client.generate(req)
    if(res.status===429){
      const delay = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after']||res.headers['x-rw-retry']||'1')
      await sleep(delay*1000*Math.pow(2,i))
      continue
    }
    return res
  }
  throw new Error('rate limited')
}
```
Owen (Runtime): Note: runtime emits resume_token in stream footer when we preemptively truncate. Recommend resuming with that token to avoid redoing compute; pass kv_cache_hint when possible.
Rex (Eng Docs): Add one-line guidance: "Prefer model-variant fallbacks for bulk jobs; prefer trimming recent context to preserve UX in live chats."
